## Claim
Text: "Hunter Biden, son of US President Joe Biden has died."
Claim date: October 25, 2020
Claim origin: https://web.archive.org/web/20210116153238/https://media.thedonald.win/post/H3A2atAb.png

## Initial Q&A
### Did Hunter Biden die on or before October 25, 2020?
Answer: No, Hunter Biden did not die on or before October 25, 2020. The claim is false; as USA Today reported on October 27, 2020, "there is no proof to support the claim that Hunter Biden is dead," and the rumor originated as a hoax on 4chan.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Is there any credible news report from a major media outlet (e.g., Associated Press, Reuters, CNN) that confirms the death of Hunter Biden as of October 25, 2020?
Answer: No, there is no credible news report from a major media outlet confirming the death of Hunter Biden as of October 25, 2020. On the contrary, USA Today published a fact-check on October 27, 2020, stating that the claim is false and originated as a 4chan hoax, citing sources such as the Associated Press, Lead Stories, and Heavy that all found no evidence to support it.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Was Hunter Biden alive and publicly active after October 25, 2020 (e.g., attending events, posting on social media, or being mentioned in news)?
Answer: Yes, Hunter Biden was alive and publicly active after October 25, 2020. The search result from RadarOnline includes numerous articles dated after that time, such as reports of him and his wife grabbing ice cream in Malibu, attending White House events, and being involved in ongoing legal and media scrutiny, all of which confirm his continued presence in public life.

Source URL: https://radaronline.com/t/hunter-biden/?page=6

### What is the original source of the claim that Hunter Biden died, and is that source known for spreading misinformation or satire?
Answer: The original source of the claim that Hunter Biden died is a post on 4chan, specifically on the "Politically Incorrect" board, made on October 25, 2020. 4chan is widely known for spreading misinformation and hoaxes, not satire, as confirmed by fact-checkers like USA Today, Lead Stories, and Heavy.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Did any government agency (e.g., the U.S. State Department or local authorities) report the death of Hunter Biden on October 25, 2020?
Answer: No government agency (such as the U.S. State Department or local authorities) reported the death of Hunter Biden on October 25, 2020; the USA Today fact-check explicitly states the rumor is false, originated as a 4chan hoax, and notes that Joe Biden was seen publicly attending church and a virtual concert that day, with no official death report.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Was Joe Biden the U.S. President on October 25, 2020, or was he still a presidential candidate at that time?
Answer: On October 25, 2020, Joe Biden was still a presidential candidate, not the U.S. President; he became the 46th president on January 20, 2021, as stated in the source: "Joe Biden ... became the 46th president of the United States on January 20, 2021."

Source URL: https://www.history.com/topics/us-presidents/joe-biden

### Did any reputable fact-checking organization (e.g., Snopes, PolitiFact) investigate and debunk the claim that Hunter Biden died on October 25, 2020?
Answer: Yes, reputable fact-checking organizations investigated and debunked the claim. USA Today reported that "both Lead Stories and Heavy also concluded that the claim is false," and the article itself states "Based on our research, the claim that Hunter Biden has died is FALSE." Lead Stories and Heavy are established fact-checking outlets that published their own debunks on October 26, 2020.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Are there any photographs, videos, or public records showing Hunter Biden alive after October 25, 2020, that contradict the claim of his death?
Answer: Yes, there are multiple public records and reports showing Hunter Biden alive after October 25, 2020. For example, the USA Today fact-check notes that on October 25, 2020, Joe Biden "attended church in Wilmington, Delaware, with his granddaughters and appeared at a virtual concert later that night," and on subsequent days he campaigned, with no evidence of Hunter Biden's death. The article explicitly states, "There is no proof to support the claim that Hunter Biden is dead," and concludes the rumor is a "4chan hoax."

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

## Final Judgement
The fact-checking evidence clearly shows that the claim of Hunter Biden's death on or before October 25, 2020, originated as a hoax on 4chan and was thoroughly debunked by multiple reputable fact-checking organizations, including USA Today, Lead Stories, and Heavy. No credible news reports, government agencies, or official sources confirmed the death, and Hunter Biden was publicly active after that date, as evidenced by news articles and his father's public appearances. The evidence explicitly and clearly refutes the claim.

